Prepare project report – Document the project objectives, scope, methodology, and outcomes.

Document requirements – Record functional and non-functional requirements.

Document system design – Include architecture, flowcharts, UML diagrams, database design, and interface designs.

Document development process – Explain the technologies, tools, programming methods, and implementation steps used.

Document testing – Record test cases, test results, errors found, and corrections made.

Prepare user documentation – Provide instructions explaining how users can operate the system.

Prepare technical documentation – Provide information that helps developers maintain or modify the system.

Record project results – Describe the final outcome, achievements, limitations, and possible improvements.

Organize references – List books, websites, research papers, tools, and other sources used.
